<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine peso closes higher after weak opening.</title>
<headline>Philippine peso closes higher after weak opening.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- Nov 28 -------------------------</p>
<p>	    * Central Bank lowers selling rate</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine peso settled higher at 26.282 to the dollar, recovering from a weak opening after demand for dollars eased by mid-morning, traders said.</p>
<p>The peso slipped to an intra-day low of 26.292 in early trade, down from Thursday's close of 26.288, as foreign banks shifted their portfolio out of peso-denominated instruments due to the softening of domestic interest rates.</p>
</text>
